silm:instances_papers_03_silmaril_federation_chapters_10_cross_paper_bridges_sections_01_bridge_to_yoneda_lemma_concrete_anchor_mittens_node silm:hasExample "In 'MittensInFederationOlog', the bare-symbol→anchor table grounds the abstract symbols in the Tartu-Animal-Clinic / Mittens-2026-05-18 domain story. For example, Mittens is the concrete cat individual entered as a federation object. In the diagram, this node represents the governed individual whose vet records, storage packets, and catalog traces are the cocone legs. A distributed-systems engineer reads this as 'the primary key around which all replicas converge.'." .
